{
    "title": "An autosave that cancels itself",
    "summary": "A draft saved a second after the typing stops, with the cancel as the effect's return value. Replay to watch nineteen keystrokes become one save, then change the topic.",
    "files": [
        "src/ui/pages/editor/page.abide",
        "src/ui/session.ts",
        "src/server/rpc/drafts.ts"
    ],
    "route": "/editor",
    "states": [
        { "id": "typing1", "file": "typing1.html", "hold": 500, "after": "typing2" },
        { "id": "typing2", "file": "typing2.html", "hold": 500, "after": "typing3" },
        { "id": "typing3", "file": "typing3.html", "hold": 900, "after": "saving" },
        { "id": "saving", "file": "saving.html", "hold": 600, "after": "saved" },
        {
            "id": "saved",
            "file": "saved.html",
            "on": {
                "change [data-topic]": "switched"
            }
        },
        {
            "id": "switched",
            "file": "switched.html",
            "on": {
                "change [data-topic]": "saved"
            }
        }
    ],
    "bench": {
        "note": "AUTHORED, not measured — nothing here runs until the compiler does. LINES OF CODE IS THE EXCEPTION: counted from the two arms in this download, code lines only, both arms complete — markup, client and handler. It comes out LEVEL — slightly against, in fact, this arm carrying a second watch the hand-written one has no place to put. A `clearTimeout` is one line; the rows above it are where the difference is.",
        "rows": [
            {
                "metric": "Saves over nineteen keystrokes",
                "abide": "1",
                "vanilla": "1",
                "ratio": "1.00x"
            },
            {
                "metric": "Analytics calls over the same nineteen",
                "abide": "1",
                "vanilla": "1",
                "ratio": "1.00x"
            },
            {
                "metric": "Analytics calls, with `sources` removed",
                "abide": "20",
                "vanilla": "1",
                "ratio": "20.00x"
            },
            {
                "metric": "Teardown paths written",
                "abide": "0",
                "vanilla": "2",
                "ratio": "0.00x"
            },
            {
                "metric": "Client bytes",
                "abide": "3.8 kB",
                "vanilla": "1.8 kB",
                "ratio": "2.11x"
            },
            {
                "metric": "Lines of code",
                "abide": "42",
                "vanilla": "40",
                "ratio": "1.05x"
            }
        ]
    },
    "tests": {
        "note": "`bun test examples/watching`. Every row counts RUNS rather than reading the page: an autosave that leaked a timer and one that cancelled it save the same draft.",
        "rows": [
            {
                "name": "a rerun runs the previous run's disposer before the effect",
                "result": "pass"
            },
            {
                "name": "the last disposer runs once at teardown",
                "result": "pass"
            },
            {
                "name": "a tracked effect wakes on every value its body read",
                "result": "pass"
            },
            {
                "name": "`sources` narrows an effect to the values it names",
                "result": "pass"
            },
            {
                "name": "a watch from a plain module stops on the disposer it handed back",
                "result": "pass"
            },
            {
                "name": "an effect that throws stops its watch and reaches `onError`",
                "result": "pass"
            }
        ]
    },
    "wire": [
        {
            "request": "POST /__abide/rpc/drafts/saveDraft",
            "requestHeaders": {
                "content-type": "application/json",
                "cookie": "abide-caller=Vd3kPq1sLm9xR2tAj7Nc4Q"
            },
            "status": "200 OK",
            "responseHeaders": {
                "content-type": "application/json",
                "cache-control": "private, no-store"
            },
            "body": "{\n    \"ok\": true\n}"
        }
    ],
    "vanilla": [
        "index.html",
        "editor.js",
        "server.ts"
    ]
}
